{
  "about": "score{} voice allocation, shared by the engine (tests/kit.rs) and the web panel's TS mirror. Ticks are 4 ms (timer(0, 32)); step = a 16th = 3750/tempo ticks; step index i is 0-based and counts across the whole arrangement (patterns concatenated in arrangement order); start(i) = floor((i + (swing/100 if i odd else 0)) * step + 0.5); a hit (1-4) holds through following '-' chars in the same string and ends at start(index of the first non-'-' step after it, or of the pattern's end) \u2014 holds never cross a pattern boundary; a '-' with no hit (or hold) immediately before it is a setup error; events are produced and allocated in order (slot, step, row), which equals (start, row) because tempo is capped at 400; each event's voice = the lowest voice 0..7 whose most recent note (after any cut) has end <= this start; if none, steal the voice whose most recent note has the smallest start (lowest voice on a tie) and set that note's end to this start (it may become zero-length); rows are 1-based; length = start(total steps).",
